r more failed transactions, Degraded = at least one with 1 % or more, Healthy otherwise; worst first. A service needs at least 20 transactions in the hour to be rated (fewer = "Low traffic", shown in the services list but not counted here, so one failed call out of two does not make an application Failing). Failing / Degraded = how many of its services; Worst = the worst service's error rate; App = the application's overall error rate. To see which services, pick the application in the Application control: "Services of the Application" lists them. Click an application to open it in the ServiceNow CMDB. From the APM CMDB enrichment on each service (398 of 400 production services carry their application, round 10). Servers: the hosts its services' APM agents reported from in the last 15 minutes (up to 3, then "+N more"; "—" = no APM agent host data). Type one into the Server control to see its health. Health covers the last hour and Servers the last 15 minutes (both set in the query). The panel shows "Last 5 years" only for the CMDB links of the selected CI, which ServiceNow re-sends only when they change; APM data is never read further back than the last hour.", "hide_title": false, "attributes": {"title": "Application Health", "references": [], "state": {"datasourceStates": {"textBased": {"layers": {"879814b0-795b-563a-a673-fda73b4ead28": {"index": "d5d05296586503175cd7c6a97af9340c504a97756a7b75988072c886bdf0dc39", "query": {"esql": "FROM metrics-apm.service_transaction.1m-*, metrics-apm.internal-*, cmdb-ci-relations* METADATA _index
